{"name":"Maggie’s Magic","hex":"#ddeee2","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maggie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several kinds of bird in the family Corvidae, especially Pica pica.","A superficially similar Australian bird, Gymnorhina tibicen or Cracticus tibicen."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maggie"},{"term":"magic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The application of rituals or actions, especially those based on occult knowledge, to subdue or manipulate natural or supernatural beings and forces in order to have some benefit from them. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","The supernatural forces which are drawn on in such a ritual."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having supernatural talents, properties or qualities attributed to magic.","Producing extraordinary results, as though through the use of magic."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/magic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Maggie's","blocks":[{"text":"Maggie's centres are a network of drop-in centres across the United Kingdom and abroad that aim to help anyone who has been affected by cancer. They are intended as welcoming and caring environments that provide support, information and practical advice to people dealing with a cancer diagnosis. They also offer wellbeing sessions and workshops to complement conventional cancer therapy."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/Maggie%27s_logo.png/330px-Maggie%27s_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maggie's","wikidata":"Q3843132"},{"title":"Maggie","blocks":[{"text":"Maggie or Maggy is a feminine given name. It can be a short form of Magdalena, Magnolia, Margaret, or Marigold."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maggie","wikidata":"Q1625970"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/76/Maggie_Jencks_statue_%40_Maggie